A //plumb: directive floating free between declarations attaches to no node’s
doc comment, so plumb’s targeted scan would skip it; the full-file sweep reports
it instead. (The blank line keeps it from attaching to the following var as its
doc comment.)
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrMisplacedDirective
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type T struct{}

//plumb:build
func New() *T { return &T{} }

//plumb:build

var x = 1
